## What Affects Renovation Costs in Vancouver?

Several factors influence your final renovation cost:

1. **Scope of work:** A cosmetic update costs far less than a structural renovation. Moving walls, plumbing, or electrical adds significant cost.
2. **Material selection:** Builder-grade laminate countertops vs premium quartz, stock cabinets vs custom — materials can account for 40–60% of your budget.
3. **Property type:** Condo renovations may require strata approval and are limited to certain construction hours. See our guide to [BC Strata Renovation Rules](/en/blog/strata-renovation-rules-vancouver/) for Metro Vancouver homeowners. Heritage homes may need specialized materials and techniques.
4. **Permits:** Structural, plumbing, and electrical work all require permits in Metro Vancouver. Our [Critical Load Panel Installation](/en/services/critical-load-panel/) service upgrades your home electrical capacity for modern renovation demands. Permit fees range from $200–$2,000 depending on scope.
5. **Location within Metro Vancouver:** West Vancouver and Vancouver West Side projects tend to cost 10–20% more due to higher material expectations and access logistics.
6. **Market conditions:** Contractor availability, lumber prices, and supply chain factors all influence pricing. Get quotes from multiple contractors and compare line-by-line.

