## Frequently Asked Questions

### How much does a home renovation cost in Vancouver in 2026?

Renovation costs in Metro Vancouver vary widely by scope. Budget benchmarks from real 2026 projects: **kitchen renovation** $15,000–$72,000+ (average mid-range: $32,000); **bathroom renovation** $10,000–$60,000+ (average mid-range: $22,000); **basement finish** $30,000–$90,000 (legal suite: $70,000–$120,000); **whole-house renovation** $80,000–$300,000+; **painting whole interior** $4,000–$12,000; **flooring replacement** (1,000 sqft) $5,000–$25,000. The biggest cost variable in any renovation: whether structural changes, plumbing/electrical relocation, or permits are involved. Cosmetic-only work costs 30–50% less than full gut renovations.

### What is the biggest cost driver in Vancouver renovations?

Labour is the largest cost component in Metro Vancouver renovation budgets — typically 40–55% of total project cost. Skilled trades in Vancouver command $85–$150/hour (plumbers, electricians, tile setters). Cabinet and countertop material selection is the second biggest variable in kitchen renovations. Permit requirements and structural changes (load-bearing wall removal, foundation waterproofing) are the most unpredictable cost items — each can add $8,000–$30,000 depending on the extent of work. Material lead times (6–12 weeks for custom cabinets, 3–6 weeks for engineered hardwood) can also extend timelines and affect project costs through carrying costs.

### How accurate are online renovation cost calculators for Vancouver?

Online renovation cost calculators are useful for ballpark estimates (within ±30–40%) but often underestimate Vancouver costs by 20–40% because: (1) they use national averages, not Metro Vancouver''s labour market (one of Canada''s highest); (2) they don''t account for Vancouver-specific permit costs and processing times; (3) they don''t reflect Vancouver''s material supply chain (imported materials face longer lead times and higher shipping costs). For an accurate estimate, get 2–3 itemized quotes from licensed Metro Vancouver contractors. Reno Stars provides free detailed written quotes — no obligation, response within 24 hours.

### Why are renovation costs higher in Vancouver than the rest of Canada?

Metro Vancouver renovation costs run 25–40% above the Canadian national average due to: (1) Labour market — skilled trades earn $35–$75/hour in Vancouver vs. $25–$55 in most Canadian cities; (2) Higher cost of living affects contractor overhead; (3) Permit fees and processing time add administrative costs; (4) Building code requirements (seismic standards, mould prevention) in BC often exceed other provinces; (5) Material costs are higher due to transportation to a coastal market; (6) Demand — Metro Vancouver''s real estate values make renovation financially viable at higher spend levels than most markets. Reno Stars operates exclusively in Metro Vancouver and prices reflect actual local market conditions.

### How do I budget for unexpected costs in a Vancouver renovation?

Budget a 10–20% contingency above your renovation contract price for unforeseen costs. The most common unexpected costs in Metro Vancouver renovations: (1) Hidden water damage or mould (found after tile or drywall removal) — $3,000–$15,000 remediation; (2) Outdated electrical (knob-and-tube wiring requiring upgrade) — $8,000–$20,000; (3) Asbestos in pre-1990 homes (stippled ceilings, floor tiles, pipe insulation) — $2,000–$8,000 abatement; (4) Framing deficiencies requiring structural repair; (5) Unforeseen plumbing issues (galvanized pipes, cast iron drain with root infiltration). Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping. Reno Stars documents all discoveries in writing before proceeding with any scope change — nothing additional is added without your signed change order.

