### What questions should I ask during a Vancouver renovation contractor site visit?
A site visit is your best opportunity to assess a contractor''s knowledge and approach. Key questions to ask: (1) Have you completed projects like mine specifically — same home type, similar scope, same neighbourhood? (2) Who are the specific tradespeople (plumber, electrician) you use, and are they licensed BC tradespeople? (3) What is your project management approach — who is my single point of contact throughout the project? (4) What does your payment schedule look like, and is it tied to specific milestones? (5) What happens if hidden issues are discovered behind walls during demolition — how are change orders handled and priced? The answers to these questions reveal far more about a contractor''s professionalism than their marketing materials do.


