</ul>
<p><strong>Plumbing work</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Relocate or replace supply and drain lines as required</li>
<li>Install new shower valve, tub filler, or faucet</li>
<li>Rough-in for any relocated fixtures</li>
<li>Pressure test before closing walls</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Tile and waterproofing</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Floor tile installation (heated floor optional)</li>
<li>Shower or tub surround tile (floor-to-ceiling is the standard in Burnaby condos)</li>
<li>Grout sealing</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Fixtures and finishing</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Vanity installation with undermount or integrated sink</li>
<li>Mirror or medicine cabinet</li>
<li>Lighting — potlights, vanity bar, or feature lighting</li>
<li>Towel bars, toilet paper holder, hooks</li>
<li>Toilet installation (optional — most clients keep the existing toilet if it&#39;s in good condition)</li>
</ul>
<h2>Strata Requirements for Burnaby Condos and Townhouses</h2>
<p>Most Burnaby bathroom renovations require strata approval before work begins. Our [cabinet refinishing](/en/services/cabinet/) service can transform your cabinets without full replacement. Here&#39;s what the strata typically requires:</p>
<ol>
