## Frequently Asked Questions

### How much does a bathroom renovation cost in Burnaby in 2026?

Bathroom renovation costs in Burnaby run $12,000–$48,000 for a typical renovation, consistent with Metro Vancouver averages. Tier breakdown: (1) **Budget refresh** ($12,000–$18,000) — stock vanity, basic tile, updated fixtures, same layout; common for rental properties and pre-sale updates; (2) **Mid-range renovation** ($18,000–$32,000) — semi-custom vanity, large-format tile, glass shower or frameless enclosure, heated floor, new fixtures throughout; (3) **High-end** ($35,000–$55,000+) — custom millwork, freestanding soaker tub, walk-in shower, premium tile, in-floor heat, statement lighting. Labour and permit costs in Burnaby are equivalent to other Metro Vancouver municipalities. Reno Stars has completed 25+ bathroom renovations in Burnaby since 2021.

### How long does a bathroom renovation take in Burnaby?

Timeline for a Burnaby bathroom renovation: permit processing (if required) 4–8 weeks concurrent with design; demolition 1–2 days; rough-in plumbing and electrical 2–4 days; waterproofing and cement board 1 day; tile 3–5 days; vanity, toilet, fixtures 1–2 days; glass shower door 1 day; final grouting and caulking 1 day. Total construction time: 10–18 business days. Like-for-like fixture swaps with no layout change (no permit needed) complete in 8–12 business days. Full renovation with permit: 8–14 weeks total (including permit wait). Reno Stars provides a day-by-day schedule at the time of contract signing.

### Do I need a permit for a bathroom renovation in Burnaby?

A building permit from the City of Burnaby is required for bathroom renovations that involve: moving or adding drain lines, new electrical circuits, structural wall changes, or adding a new bathroom. Like-for-like fixture replacement (toilet, vanity, faucet, at the same locations) does NOT require a permit. A plumbing permit (ESA) is required any time a licensed plumber is doing drain or supply work beyond fixture replacement. Burnaby permit fees for a typical $20,000 bathroom renovation: $350–$600 (building) + $200–$350 (plumbing/electrical if applicable). Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping. Reno Stars determines permit requirements at the initial site visit and handles applications on the client''s behalf.

### What tile is best for a Burnaby bathroom renovation?

Most popular tile choices for Burnaby bathroom renovations in 2026: (1) **Large-format porcelain (24×24 or 12×24)** — most popular for floors and wet wall areas; minimal grout, easy clean; (2) **Subway tile (4×12 or 3×6 in stacked bond)** — timeless for shower walls; vertical stack adds height; (3) **Terrazzo-look tile** — on trend in Burnaby''s contemporary new builds and renovations; (4) **Hexagon mosaic (2" or 4")** — for shower floors or accent strips; (5) **Fluted/ribbed tile** — on trend for feature walls and vanity backs. Burnaby''s high-density condo market favours large-format, light-toned tile for its space-amplifying effect. Reno Stars sources tile from Burnaby-local suppliers to minimize lead times.

### Is there a Burnaby strata approval process for bathroom renovations?

Yes — if your Burnaby property is a strata (condo or townhouse), you need strata council approval before starting any bathroom renovation, even cosmetic work. Requirements vary by strata bylaws but typically include: written application with scope of work, contractor credentials (Consumer Protection BC license number, WCB clearance letter, $2M+ CGL insurance certificate naming the strata as additional insured), and confirmation of work hours compliance (most Burnaby stratas restrict work to Monday–Friday, 8 AM–5 PM). Allow 2–6 weeks for approval. Reno Stars provides the complete strata package for Burnaby condo clients — we''ve worked with 15+ different Burnaby strata corporations.

