### What bathroom renovation scope is most popular for Burnaby homeowners in 2026?

The most popular bathroom renovation scope for Burnaby homeowners combines a tub-to-shower conversion with full tile replacement. Entry-level Burnaby bathroom renovations ($20,000–$25,000) typically include: removing the original 1980s or 1990s tub/surround, installing a walk-in shower with frameless glass, replacing the vanity and toilet, retiling the floor, and updating lighting. Our [Accessible Bathroom Renovation](/en/services/accessible-bathroom/) service specialises in safety upgrades and accessibility modifications. This scope addresses the three most common buyer concerns in Burnaby''s single-family market: dated tub surround, original vanity, and old tile. For Burnaby condos, the same scope runs $22,000–$28,000 due to strata material disposal requirements and elevator protection. See our guide to [BC Strata Renovation Rules](/ru/blog/strata-renovation-rules-vancouver/) for Metro Vancouver homeowners.

